{"author":{"id":"7c5527b9befade3b1be0c1d677ac996815288d8332f34269730a5b81425ee5be"},"ops":[{"type":5,"timestamp":1791208847,"nonce":"Xe4BkWv2qk2M3z+GgtoHz2FeKBo=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"LE_lADOULtcMc8AAAABVIseHc8AAAAHkgexRA","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:labels":"refactor"},"added":["refactor"],"removed":[]},{"type":6,"timestamp":1791272562,"nonce":"917kXCd+NULGqZp+3poPzRS5koU=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"UCE_lAHOULtcMc8AAAABVIseHc7-YJ94","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:text":"ba939487f8c164fa0104b1e2f4f6ed5a4c679ac52d692c60a902a3d2b1eb2328"},"target":"d68aebe41c1375dc6eb27985b092da2f9736f3bc07acc9c0b4351c2fb773cc12","message":"**TL;DR**\n- **What:** remove the Kubernetes deployment.\n- **Why:** we only use GitHub Pages, and the other one costs maintenance for nothing.\n- **User impact:** none.\n- **Effort:** small.\n\n---\n\n**Is your feature request related to a problem? Please describe.**\nMITSI currently has two production targets:\n\n- `.github/workflows/pages.yml` publishes `main` to GitHub Pages (#4).\n- `.github/workflows/deploy.yml` builds a Docker image and deploys `dev`, `stage` and `v*.*.*` tags to the ENAC Kubernetes cluster through `EPFL-ENAC/epfl-enac-build-push-deploy-action@v3.1.0`.\n\nWe deploy to GitHub Pages, so the Kubernetes path is dead weight:\n\n- It builds and pushes an image on every push to `dev` and needs the `CD_TOKEN` secret.\n- It keeps `frontend/Dockerfile`, `nginx.conf` and `entrypoint.sh` alive.\n- It triggers on `stage`, a branch that doesn't exist.\n- The READMEs describe a `dev` → `stage` → `main` flow that doesn't match what we do: #26 merged `dev` straight into `main`.\n\n**Describe the solution you'd like**\n- [ ] Record in #31 that GitHub Pages is the only production target.\n- [ ] Delete `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`.\n- [ ] Decide what happens to `frontend/Dockerfile`, `frontend/nginx.conf` and `frontend/entrypoint.sh`:\n  - delete them (git history keeps them if we ever need them again), **or**\n  - keep them on purpose for local container use, and clean them up as described in the build-cleanup issue.\n- [ ] Ask ENAC-IT to remove the `epfl-vps/mitsi` overlays in `enack8s-app-config` and the running `dev` deployment, and delete the published `ghcr.io` images.\n- [ ] Update the \"Deployment\" section of the root `README.md` and \"Production builds\" in `frontend/README.md`.\n- [ ] Define the Pages release flow. Today every push to `main` publishes. Do the `v0.1.0` and `v0.1.1` tags still mean anything? Is `stage` coming back?\n\n**Describe alternatives you've considered**\nKeep Kubernetes as production and drop Pages. This contradicts #4 and the direction of #31.\n\n**Additional context**\nRaised in an architecture review of `dev` at `b35fc8c`. Image vulnerability scanning in the CI issue only applies if the Docker path is kept.","files":null},{"type":2,"timestamp":1791272562,"nonce":"6oWZedKx0WBakF/qrRTgzhMaocQ=","metadata":{"sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:id":"RTE_lADOULtcMc8AAAABVIseHc8AAAAHlcnErg","sync:github.com/epfl-enac/vps-mitsi:title":"[TASK](Deployment) Keep only the GitHub Pages deployment"},"title":"[TASK](Deployment) Keep only the GitHub Pages deployment","was":"[CHORE](Deployment) Remove the Kubernetes deploy workflow, GitHub Pages is the target"}]}